1. What is the purpose of functions?
- Functions provide for the storing of instructions in memory. They help reduce code duplication.
- Functions allow you to re use code, allows you to organize your code into smaller and more manageable blocks.
- Functions in JavaScript are used to group code into reusable blocks.
- It can take in parameters and return values. It can allow you to control the scope of variables.
- They also improve readability of code

2. Differentiate between a parameter and an argument.
- A parameter is where you would specify the data that must be input into the function.
- An argument is the value you would pass into the function.
    - e.g. parameter = food & argument = "burger"

