8. Write some pseudocode to describe the following problem:
We want to be able to split a string by some delimiter to create an array of values, e.g. the string
"Dave,Smith,67" would be split by commas to create an array that contains three values.

//Miguel example

SET I to 0
SET array to []
INPUT SplitWord from keyboard
FUNCTION with SplitWord as parameter
	WHILE SplitWord length > 0
		IF SplitWord Includes ,
			COMPUTE find first comma and store all characters before the comma to array[i]
			COMPUTE delete the comma and all characters before the comma
 			SET ARRAY[i] + 1 to “”
			COMPUTE i + 1
		ELSE
			COMPUTE array[i] EQUALS SplitWord
		ENDIF
	ENDWHILE
ENDFUNCTION



